{% from '_macros.j2' import section %}
{{ section(idx, finding, severity_label, repro_curl,
    impact=(
"The endpoint returns CORS headers that allow credentialed cross-origin reads from origins the application "
"should not trust. Concrete attack: an attacker-controlled origin can make authenticated requests on behalf "
"of a logged-in victim (using their session cookie / bearer token), read the response, and exfiltrate it. "
"Impact compounds with any endpoint that returns sensitive data (PII, tokens, account state). For null-origin "
"or `*`-with-credentials misconfigurations, every cross-site script or sandboxed iframe becomes an exfil channel."
),
    validation=(
"1. Replay the request with `Origin: https://attacker.example.com` and inspect the response headers. The finding "
"   is real only if `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` reflects the attacker origin **and** `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n"
"2. Confirm the endpoint actually returns sensitive data when called with valid credentials — a CORS-misconfig on "
"   a public-info endpoint is not payable.\n"
"3. Build a minimal HTML PoC (single `fetch()` with credentials) that demonstrates exfil to the attacker origin.\n"
"4. **Do not** test the PoC against a real user's session unless you control both sides. Test in your own browser "
"   with your own session cookie."
),
    note=(
"Programs reward CORS findings tied to **specific sensitive endpoints**, not site-wide policies. \"GET /api/account "
"is exfiltrable\" is paid; \"the app sets CORS wrong\" is closed informational."
)
) }}
